# COMPAT-01 (issue #472): make the "engines" floor in package.json actually
# enforced. Yarn Classic (v1) does not check "engines" by default -- without
# this, the field is decorative. engine-strict makes `yarn install` refuse a
# Node/Yarn outside the declared range instead of silently proceeding, both
# locally and in CI (see docs/development/supported-runtime-matrix.md).
engine-strict true
